Subject: scroll thumb: geometry only while the thumb is visible

What: createScrollThumb (scroll-view-thumb.ts) derives the thumb's geometry only
while it is visible (hovered, scrolled by input, or dragged): becoming visible
measures the viewport once, a resize of the viewport or its first child re-reads
the extent, and a scroll moves the thumb from that extent and scrollTop. While
hidden it reads and writes nothing. ScrollView draws its thumb with it, and
ScrollThumb (scroll-thumb.tsx, scroll-thumb.css) draws the same thumb over any
element that scrolls itself. The thumb stays mounted and is `hidden` while nothing
overflows: mounting it after the scroller flips the scroller's `:last-child`, and
markdown `> *:last-child` rules then restyled the whole subtree (651 elements on
every Collapse all in the Review).
Why: the previous thumb wrote its geometry 608 times per streamed turn, each write
after a forced layout read; a transcript growing under a streaming reply now
costs the thumb nothing.

